# A rule whose reactant pattern has a molecule joined to the rest by "." alone,
# where a complex holds more than one molecule that can be it.
#
# Cut deletes the A-B bond and writes "A.C + B", with C joined to A.B by "."
# only. BioNetGen gives each complex one reaction at rate k, however many C
# could stand for the C of the pattern, as long as one of them ends up with A.
#
# One has one C, bonded to A. Two has two C, both bonded to A, told apart by
# their state. Split has one C bonded to A and one bonded to B. Each is cut at
# rate k = 1, so 100 exp(-1) = 36.8 of each are left at t = 1. BioNetGen's ODE
# gives that for all three.
#
# A mapping for the "." molecule makes each candidate C a match of its own, and
# Two was cut at rate 2k (13.5 left), with or without -no-bscb.

begin model
begin parameters
  k  1.0
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b,c1,c2)
  B(a,c)
  C(a,t~1~2)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b!1,c1!2,c2).B(a!1,c).C(a!2,t~1)                       100
  A(b!1,c1!2,c2!3).B(a!1,c).C(a!2,t~1).C(a!3,t~2)          100
  A(b!1,c1,c2!2).B(a!1,c!3).C(a!2,t~2).C(a!3,t~2)          100
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  One    A(b!+,c1!+,c2)
  Molecules  Two    A(b!+,c1!+,c2!+)
  Molecules  Split  A(b!+,c1,c2!+)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  Cut: A(b!1).B(a!1).C() -> A(b).C() + B(a)   k
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
